{
  "tema": 5845,
  "slug": "pague",
  "titulo": "-gar verbs in the preterite",
  "subtitulo": "Pagué la cuenta; ella llegó tarde.",
  "foto": "t08.jpg",
  "regla": "In the preterite, -ar verbs ending in -gar change g to gu in the yo form only (pagué, llegué, jugué) to keep the hard g sound. All other forms are regular: pagaste, pagó.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Verbs ending in **-gar** are regular -ar verbs in the preterite, with **one spelling change**: in **yo**, the **g** becomes **gu**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Why? **ge** sounds like a harsh _h_. To keep the hard _g_ of _go_ before **é**, Spanish writes **gué**: **pagué**. The **u** is silent."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "pagar",
            "llegar",
            "jugar"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "pagué",
              "llegué",
              "jugué"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "pagaste",
              "llegaste",
              "jugaste"
            ],
            [
              "él / ella / usted",
              "pagó",
              "llegó",
              "jugó"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros / nosotras",
              "pagamos",
              "llegamos",
              "jugamos"
            ],
            [
              "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
              "pagaron",
              "llegaron",
              "jugaron"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Common ones: **pagar**, **llegar**, **jugar**, **entregar**, **apagar**, **cargar**, **pegar**, **navegar**, **colgar**, **negar**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Jugar** and **colgar** change their stem in the present (**juego**, **cuelgo**), but **not** in the preterite: **jugué**, **colgó**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: the **u** in **gué** is a bodyguard. It keeps the e from softening the g."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Pagué== la renta ayer.",
